1
00:00:00,291 --> 00:00:01,333
[ARIEL]
Sorry, Pearl.

2
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:03,545
He doesn't owe
me an explanation.

3
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:04,963
Pearl doesn't seem okay.

4
00:00:05,004 --> 00:00:07,006
Tantan, she’s fine.

5
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:08,632
Join us tomorrow
at Cabitoonan, okay?

6
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,968
- We're planting mangroves.
- Sure.

7
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:14,096
[ARIEL] Let’s go! One, two, three!
Let's start planting!

8
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,474
- [CAROL] Let’s go!
- [CROWD CHEERING]

9
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:19,102
[JAO] You know, Kara,
you should plant the first one

10
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,645
because this project won't
be possible without you.

11
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:22,771
Let Egay do it!

12
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:23,481
- Egay!
- Egay.

13
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:26,192
[KARA] Give your
mangrove a name, too.

14
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:28,611
[EGAY] How about Karajao?
Like your baby.

15
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,863
[CROWD]
Team Mangroves forever!

16
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:32,197
[CROWD CHEERING]

17
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:34,409
[CROWD CHANTING]
Team Mangroves!

18
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,118
[MAN]
Let's go!

19
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,661
[CROWD CHANTING]
Team Mangroves!

20
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:38,997
[KARA]
Who did this?

21
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:40,123
Ma’am Vida!

22
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:42,375
We got a call from
the new landowner.

23
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,667
New owner?

24
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:45,962
It had already been
sold to a corporation.

25
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:48,922
[JAO] I can already hear my
boss's voice in my head, saying...

26
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,217
that everything is
legal and aboveboard.

27
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,179
Kara, look at this.

28
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:08,735
[MIKA] Sir, please call me.
I just discovered something.

29
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:09,944
[MAN]
Jao!

30
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,405
- Sir?
- How are you?

31
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,364
[PAUL CHUCKLES]

32
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,741
What are you doing here?

33
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:15,950
Why didn't you tell me?

34
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:17,577
I have some news for you!

35
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:19,369
Couldn't you tell me
over the phone, sir?

36
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,788
You had to fly all
the way to Siargao?

37
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:21,998
Are you mad at me?

38
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,040
[JAO AND PAUL LAUGH]

39
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:25,668
No, sir.
I’m just surprised you’re here.

40
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:28,379
Well, that’s good because
I have a surprise for you.

41
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,424
You wanted to stay in
Siargao longer, right?

42
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:33,092
Sir?

43
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:38,097
See, our CEO acquired a new property
here in Barangay Cabitoonan.

44
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:39,390
In General Luna.

45
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:40,557
That’s how you
pronounce it, right?

46
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:41,768
[PAUL LAUGHS]

47
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,186
Wait, wait, sir.

48
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:45,396
Barangay Cabitoonan…

49
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:47,607
the one next to the
mangrove plantation?

50
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:48,983
Yes.

51
00:01:49,108 --> 00:01:50,777
And you’re the project lead!

52
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,488
Wait, wait, wait, sir.

53
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:55,657
Are you serious?

54
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:56,865
[PAUL LAUGHS]

55
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,284
Why would I joke
about these things?

56
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,286
Sir, that lot is
the same spot...

57
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:02,246
the locals are
fighting to protect

58
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:04,958
as part of the mangrove
reserve expansion.

59
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:08,252
You know, the upper management
is aware of all this, okay?

60
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,878
That’s why I’m here, aren’t I?

61
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:10,880
What do you mean?

62
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:13,466
They know that you’re
part of the opposing side.

63
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,300
Wait. Opposing side?

64
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:21,516
So you really see the locals defending the
mangroves of the island as the opposition?

65
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,017
Listen, okay?

66
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:28,106
Our company has the property
rights to that land, okay?

67
00:02:28,147 --> 00:02:30,649
Once we prove
regulatory compliance,

68
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:33,486
once we resolve the
dispute, this project proceeds.

69
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:36,363
Okay? That’s why I want
you and they want you

70
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,867
to stay away from the NGO
that opposes this whole project.

71
00:02:39,158 --> 00:02:40,577
Just think about it.

72
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:42,662
It’s a great opportunity.

73
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:46,291
All the socio-economic benefits
that can come from this project.

74
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:47,917
This is so good!

75
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:51,796
I can’t be part
of this project, sir.

76
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:53,173
I resign.

77
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:55,174
What?

78
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:58,176
You can’t resign!
I don’t accept your resignation!

79
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:01,764
Okay? I know you're emotional
right now, so just calm down.

80
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,266
I understand this.
But you, of all people, know

81
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,394
how important this will
be for the community!

82
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,855
We’re not doing
anything illegal.

83
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:11,357
Okay? This is aboveboard.

84
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:21,242
[ALON BY JL]

85
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:34,524
- [PHONE RINGS]
- [JAO BREATHES DEEPLY]

86
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,858
[PHONE RINGS]

87
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,568
Kara, please pick up.

88
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:42,699
[PHONE CONTINUES RINGING]

89
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:52,125
[PHONE RINGS]

90
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:53,501
Hello? Carol?

91
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:54,502
[CAROL ON THE PHONE]
Hello, Jao.

92
00:04:54,503 --> 00:04:56,713
Is Kara with you?
I can't reach her.

93
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:58,338
[CAROL ON THE PHONE]
No.

94
00:04:58,339 --> 00:04:59,881
But I ran into her earlier

95
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:02,719
when she was on her way to the
GL municipal office with Attorney Noah.

96
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:07,932
They said they were going to see the mayor
about the mangrove site in Cabitoonan.

97
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,059
Okay.
Thank you, Carol.

98
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:26,993
Is there something
you want to tell me?

99
00:05:27,201 --> 00:05:28,494
Kara, I just found out.

100
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,289
Project head?

101
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:34,625
How could you be
the project head?

102
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:39,922
- Were you even going to tell me?
- [JAO] Of course.

103
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,425
But can you please
trust me on this?

104
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:44,469
[KARA] How can I
trust you right now?

105
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,475
Kara, look.

106
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:54,854
I honestly had no idea
they’d make me project head...

107
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:57,023
for this project.

108
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:59,776
That's how my boss works.

109
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:04,488
He can assign any
development head he wants

110
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:07,492
to projects that
come under him.

111
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:12,330
I resigned as soon
as I found out, but...

112
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:14,040
he wouldn’t let me.

113
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:19,337
I also thought it might be
better if I led it because…

114
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:23,800
I can make sure that
everything is legal and...

115
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:24,926
Legal?

116
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:30,348
Do you hear yourself?

117
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:33,684
‘Cause right now,
you sound exactly like your boss.

118
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,691
[FOOTSTEPS WALKING DOWN STAIRS]

119
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,494
[NEWS REPORTER ON VIDEO]
It’s been years since

120
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:54,622
Super Typhoon Odette
devastated Siargao,

121
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:59,627
but its impact remains fresh
in the minds of Siargaonons.

122
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:07,927
Odette first made landfall on Siargao,
subjecting the island to its full force.

123
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:11,222
The storm caused over
20 billion pesos in damage...

124
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:13,224
Without those mangroves,

125
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:16,936
Typhoon Odette would have
hit the island even harder.

126
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,980
[SIARGAONON]
Exactly, Mom!

127
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:21,190
So I understand
how frustrating it is

128
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:24,402
that Jao ended up
heading the resort

129
00:07:24,443 --> 00:07:28,614
that put the mangrove
expansion on hold.

130
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:31,658
What you're feeling
right now, Kara,

131
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:33,786
must hurt worse than
getting cheated on.

132
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,413
[KARA]
Not at all.

133
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,000
I believe him when
he said he didn’t know.

134
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:41,919
So, technically,
he didn’t do anything wrong.

135
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:47,091
It's just unfortunate that,
even if it wasn't intentional,

136
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:51,304
I'm finding out that
the people I trust

137
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:53,306
are the ones who
aren't on my side.

138
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:55,641
[CAROL]
Hey! Don't say that!

139
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:59,477
Don't compare Jao to
your ex, Jeremy, okay?

140
00:07:59,478 --> 00:08:02,898
Your ex was a liar and a user.

141
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,024
Jao's different, okay?

142
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:07,153
But I can't help
having doubts.

143
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:10,364
Jao and I haven't
been together that long.

144
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:14,118
I knew Jeremy for so long,
and look what happened.

145
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:16,454
What if the same
thing happens with Jao?

146
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,124
That's why it's so
hard to trust men.

147
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:21,542
Right, Pearl?

148
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:26,172
[CAROL] Even after
my husband left me,

149
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,382
I still believe...

150
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:30,593
all men are different

151
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,261
Some are bad...

152
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:34,972
[SIARGAONON]
...but some are good.

153
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:40,353
Even if they make the same
choices or act the same way,

154
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:44,440
we have to understand
their motivations.

155
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,318
That's what really
sets them apart.

156
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,739
I was actually scared to
ask Jao which he'd choose.

157
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,783
His job or Siargao.

158
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:58,454
Kara.

159
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,749
Do you really mean
Siargao or you?

160
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,920
This is bigger than me, Pearl.

161
00:09:06,545 --> 00:09:09,548
So please,
come with me tomorrow.

162
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,885
- Of course.
- Yeah.

163
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:24,897
[ARIEL] They'll get through this
because they're Kara and Jao.

164
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,525
Right?
As in, awesome!

165
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,943
Amazing!

166
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:33,489
I don’t know.
But I understand Kara.

167
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:36,492
I actually feel bad for her.

168
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,953
[SIARGAONON]
That’s true.

169
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:55,803
[TEXT MESSAGE]
Sir Han, how are you? Are you okay?

170
00:09:56,512 --> 00:10:00,016
[TEXT MESSAGE]
Please reply.

171
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:09,442
[TEXT MESSAGE]
I hope your family’s okay. I hope you’re okay.

172
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,444
[ARIEL]
Hey.

173
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:13,654
You’re awfully quiet.

174
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:14,905
What’s going on with you?

175
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:18,451
Princess Pearl!

176
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:22,371
Hey.
You okay?

177
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:32,173
I’m already helping you out!
I don’t even work here!

178
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:39,221
[KARA]
Just think about it.

179
00:10:39,263 --> 00:10:42,349
It'll be a huge problem
once the resort is operational.

180
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,351
Exactly!

181
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:47,563
And do you know why mangroves
are so important to your community?

182
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:51,233
First of all, these trees
help hold the soil together

183
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:54,070
and prevent erosion
from the water's flow.

184
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:59,115
They also filter out dirt,
sediment, and pollutants

185
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:01,035
before they reach the sea.

186
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:02,328
But most importantly,

187
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:06,374
they're our best defense
against storms and floods.

188
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:09,877
Those trees aren't just trees.

189
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:12,712
They're protecting our community.

190
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:15,132
And they're our legacy
for the next generation.

191
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:18,551
So I hope we can all
support Project Mangrove.

192
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:22,098
And let's never
let them build that resort.

193
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,892
I hope we can count
on your support.

194
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:26,059
[MAN]
That's right.

195
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,853
I don't want another
Typhoon Odette.

196
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:31,481
[SIARGAONON]
We'll do whatever we can to help.

197
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,233
Thank you.

198
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,819
[MAN 2]
Don't worry, ma'am.

199
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:36,529
We'll help you.

200
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,779
[CROWD]
That's right!

201
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,574
All right.
We'll collect your signatures

202
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:42,325
and send them to
the Coastal Office.

203
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:43,202
[PEARL]
Here you go.

204
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,995
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

205
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:49,500
[ARIEL] Maybe you can
share these with other people.

206
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:01,679
[ARIEL] Kara's incredible, Mom.
She never gets tired.

207
00:12:01,887 --> 00:12:04,722
I think we've been to
every barangay in GL!

208
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:05,724
[CAROL CHUCKLES]

209
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:08,810
Thanks for coming with me.

210
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:11,105
Of course.
We're your sidekicks.

211
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:14,650
- Want some more?
- I'll take this.

212
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:16,193
I'm good. Thanks.

213
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,447
Jao!

214
00:12:19,488 --> 00:12:20,281
Eat!

215
00:12:20,282 --> 00:12:21,574
- [ARIEL] Jao, eat up.
- [JAO] Good evening.

216
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:24,368
[CAROL]
Get him a plate.

217
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:26,871
Aren't you getting
my messages?

218
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,497
I've been trying to
reach you all day.

219
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,292
I haven't checked
my phone.

220
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,585
I’m busy.

221
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:35,546
Thanks to your company.

222
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:40,301
I have to expedite
the mangrove permits.

223
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:45,097
Kara, can we please
be mature about this?

224
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,100
Why?
What did I say?

225
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:50,561
Are you mad at me?

226
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:52,646
Are you going to
argue with me?

227
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:53,981
If I need to.

228
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,234
Jao, I can’t let this pass.

229
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:58,777
Kara, you have to trust me.

230
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:02,573
This project can’t
move forward, Jao.

231
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:05,117
Hey, it's not that simple.
I know my boss.

232
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:07,786
He always finds workarounds
to make things happen.

233
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:09,705
Are you afraid of him?

234
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:11,749
Why would I be afraid?

235
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:14,376
I'm just being rational
and professional about this!

236
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:15,920
I know what I'm doing!

237
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:20,591
And you know
where I stand, right?

238
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:24,929
Hey, wait.

239
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:26,555
[SIARGAONON]
That's enough.

240
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,641
Don’t fight.

241
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:31,810
[CAROL] You two aren't the
ones who get to decide this!

242
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,815
[CAROL] Better yet,
let's set up a meeting

243
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:39,776
with the locals
affected by this.

244
00:13:39,777 --> 00:13:41,779
I'll talk to the captain, okay?

245
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,866
[CAROL] Let's hear
what the people think.

246
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:48,035
Listen to them first.

247
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:51,205
Instead of...
arguing with each other.

248
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,165
Good idea.

249
00:13:57,294 --> 00:13:58,504
You should eat.

250
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,008
We still have fish.

251
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:15,187
[ARIEL IN SIARGAONON]
Thank you so much for coming, everyone.

252
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,397
Thank you also
to Captain Gani

253
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:20,526
for helping organize
this meeting.

254
00:14:20,609 --> 00:14:25,738
We're here to hear from
the residents of Cabitoonan

255
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:32,371
about the proposed luxury
resort by Young Horizon Builders,

256
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:34,622
which Pure Coast opposes.

257
00:14:34,623 --> 00:14:37,750
Pure Coast wants to
preserve the property

258
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:41,463
as part of the mangrove
reserve expansion.

259
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:46,844
Here to represent Young Horizon
Builders is Mr. Jao Calderon.

260
00:14:46,885 --> 00:14:50,054
[CLAPPING]

261
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:55,310
And representing Pure Coast
is Ms. Kara De Leon.

262
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:58,688
[CLAPPING]

263
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:00,983
Kara, Jao, please start.

264
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,192
No need to be formal.

265
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:03,235
Sounds good.

266
00:15:03,902 --> 00:15:05,779
Good afternoon, everyone.

267
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:08,490
Thank you all for coming.

268
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:11,410
It shows how much you
care about the island.

269
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:13,620
[SIARGAONON]
Good morning.

270
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,623
Kara’s right.

271
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:18,459
We're here to
hear your thoughts

272
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:22,046
on the luxury resort
proposed for Cabitoonan,

273
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:26,592
which will certainly provide
jobs for the local residents.

274
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:32,973
[OLD LADY] You two
look good together.

275
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:37,269
Oh, we're very different.
Way different.

276
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:41,190
[CROWD GIGGLING]

277
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:47,571
We hope you'll support
Pure Coast's goal

278
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:50,908
of planting more mangroves
here in Cabitoonan.

279
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:53,869
We all know how
important mangroves are

280
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:56,955
in protecting us from storms.

281
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,334
At Young Horizon Builders,

282
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:05,046
you can rest assured we'll
carefully study this project

283
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:08,967
to ensure we comply
with all environmental laws.

284
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:13,972
You can also rest assured
that we'll hire locally

285
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:19,061
for both construction
and resort operations.

286
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,691
We all know your
company's track record.

287
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,860
It can’t keep a single promise.

288
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:29,613
Sure, they'll have jobs.
But then what?

289
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,616
Will the resort protect
them when a storm hits?

290
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:35,910
[LOCAL]
Exactly! We'll have jobs,

291
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:39,330
but how can we work
if we're dead, right?

292
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:41,874
[CROWD MURMURING IN AGREEMENT]

293
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:45,546
[ARIEL] Okay...
Thank you, everyone.

294
00:16:45,587 --> 00:16:51,218
We're here to see who supports
the project and who doesn't.

295
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:54,053
[ARIEL] We'll be collecting
your signatures...

296
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,055
Good job.

297
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:59,727
Are you deliberately provoking me
to make me attack your company?

298
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:02,019
[LOCAL]
So once the resort is finished...

299
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:03,856
I'm just proud, Kara,

300
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,734
to see you fight for
what you believe in.

301
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:09,068
[BACKGROUND CHATTER]

302
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:09,945
[LOCAL]
That’s right.

303
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:13,115
But isn't it more important to
protect human lives as well as nature?

304
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,950
[CROWD MURMURING IN AGREEMENT]

305
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:20,831
[ARIEL] Okay, so for those who
agree with our appeal or protest letter...

306
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:46,023
So this is Sir Han's room.

307
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,986
You'd never guess he's rich.

308
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,542
No wonder he
always smells so good.

309
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,420
Especially his breath!

310
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,401
[ARIEL]
Life is hard,

311
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:36,156
so a lot of locals are counting
on jobs once the resort is built.

312
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:41,411
We can't judge them because
we don't know their circumstances.

313
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:46,583
We just need to make sure they
understand the consequences.

314
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,125
[ARIEL SIGHS]

315
00:18:48,126 --> 00:18:49,336
[SIARGAONON]
That's true.

316
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:52,172
You really just have to
choose your hard, right?

317
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:01,265
[PAUL]
Kara, right?

318
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:03,934
Yes?

319
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,270
I’m Paul.

320
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,063
Jao’s boss.

321
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:14,403
Excuse me.

322
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:15,529
[PAUL CLEARS THROAT]

323
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:16,196
Oh...

324
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,823
I'm not invited.

325
00:19:26,456 --> 00:19:27,583
Five million?

326
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,459
10 million.

327
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:30,878
Name your price.

328
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:51,023
You know,
in this digital age,

329
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,357
news travels fast.

330
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,816
Ms. Caitlyn De Leon?

331
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:54,942
That’s your name, right?

332
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:56,569
You can change your name

333
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,239
but the past will always
come back after you.

334
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,073
Release it.

335
00:20:00,115 --> 00:20:01,617
Make sure peak hours.

336
00:20:01,658 --> 00:20:03,327
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Oh, my god!

337
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:05,245
That woman’s just an outsider.

338
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:07,663
She doesn't care
about the island's future.

339
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,918
I think people need
to hear your side.

340
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,376
Your ally is my enemy.

341
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:15,172
You might as well tell
me you don't need me.

342
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,547
I need you.

343
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:18,550
But not for the
reasons that you think.

344
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:20,593
Headquarters asked
for your contact info.

345
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:24,806
They want to offer you the
international field officer position.

346
00:20:24,848 --> 00:20:27,642
Is that the one with
headquarters in Denmark?

347
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:29,645
You're going
international, Kara!

348
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:32,648
But if I take it,
I'll have to leave the island?
